Apache-2.0 only:

- runtime/sounds/done.mp3
- runtime/sounds/request.mp3

  herdr's assets/sounds/done.mp3 and assets/sounds/request.mp3, byte for byte, last
  changed upstream in 0403775fd2a9458417c5349d5441125ab9b2553c. They are what
  plugin.chime plays when a pane stops working or starts waiting for you.

- runtime/lua/neotmux/detect.lua

  Takes its shape from herdr: a rule with a priority, a state and the screen regions it
  reads is herdr's src/detect/manifests/*.toml, and the hold — a fall to idle disbelieved
  until it settles, unless the screen says idle in so many words — is herdr's
  src/pane/agent_detection.rs, last changed upstream in
  9c96f7ddb3be2cc575a159d4d1f1d49fb10d7006.

- runtime/lua/neotmux/agents/claude.lua

  A port of herdr's Claude Code manifest, src/detect/manifests/claude.toml, last changed
  upstream in a05c403881c5a5a6b65317d3dd349b11591fc4c6: the rules, their priorities and
  their order are herdr's reading of that program's screen. The ids are kept verbatim so
  that the two files can be read against each other, and are quoted as such in this
  repository's tests.

The three words a pane's state is spelled in — working, blocked, idle — are herdr's too.

The Cargo `license` field on every crate stays "MIT OR Apache-2.0": no crate
carries or packages any of the files above. runtime/ is installed beside the binary
(see the Makefile's install-runtime target), not compiled into or published with one.
